dev/model/evaluate.py — one script scoring all four model families (empirical
matrix / logit / best NN / 8-net ensemble) through a single path on the frozen,
unthinned per-window test slices. Produces:
  - Table B: test-year x model NLL + pooled (84,512,377 rows) + pooled-by-origin
  - AUC: one-vs-rest per (origin, destination), pooled (full 11 + key windows)
  - Calibration reliability diagrams (current->prepaid / ->dpd_30; pooled + 2020-21)
  - Predicted-vs-realized monthly rate overlay 2015-2025
  - Ensemble-size curve (paper Fig 7) from the committed key-window summaries
  -> outputs/tables/loan_level/{table_b,auc}.*, outputs/figures/loan_level/F_*,
     models/nn/full/evaluate_summary.json

All M11 Accept PASS (evaluate_summary.json):
  [1] every model on identical per-window frozen rows (row-count == committed
      metrics.json + byte-identical scaler/vocab per window; key-hash recorded)
  [2] each pooled test row appears exactly once (Sum window rows == unique
      (loan, period_ym) == 84,512,377; period_ym test bounds tile disjointly)
  [3] figures regenerate
  Headline: NN beats logit 11/11 windows; pooled NN 0.101468 < logit 0.108249
  < empirical 0.111477 (NN -9.0% vs floor vs logit -2.9%).

AUC change: _auc_one_vs_rest uses a vectorized tie-corrected average-rank
(np.unique) instead of a per-row Python loop (which did not scale to ~80M rows).
Verified equivalent before relying on it on a real 386,760-row tie-bearing slice
(384,724 unique scores): vectorized = python-loop = sklearn roc_auc_score =
0.7154566517383941, |delta| = 0.0 three-way.

